# t18-pdf-worker: what the lead applies (hot files)

## native/core/Cargo.lock (regenerate with `cargo update --workspace --offline`; no new package)
mixdog-fonts: add dependencies futures, mixdog-rt, mixdog-statefile.
mixdog-exthost-worker: add dependency reqwest (mixdog-fonts, mixdog-office-pdf were already edges).
mixdog-app-server-daemon: add dependency mixdog-fonts.
Then the hakari check for mixdog-workspace-hack (reqwest features on the worker, futures on fonts).

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json
Index the set `office-content-ops` (recorder benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-content-ops.mjs, 1 file, golden.json;
its own MANIFEST.json is in the set) with `node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs --write-index`.

## compose.rs, fn native_ext_methods
The worker's prepare_fonts now runs the Noto provisioner (mixdog_fonts::install, the one the daemon calls through
domain_seams/office_fonts.rs), so drop the document.installLibreOffice term:

    .filter(|method| !method.starts_with("image."))

(and the doc comment line about installLibreOffice).

## Test run the lead must do for the daemon (read-only edit here)
nextest run -p mixdog-app-server-daemon: domain_seams::office_fonts tests (the table, verify and prepare match Node's) after the move
to mixdog-fonts; the daemon file is now a host (asset fetcher + process manager) over mixdog_fonts::install.
